{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 12139687313118685207, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 630, "mtime": 1791872379.808898, "sha256": "bf72925d25d7cde36effbf73bec977e5a513ade57bc72aaad4057890fa56f73d"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 635, "mtime": 1791872379.812898, "sha256": "5ba84f190480a55fc24c40db64b7c4fb93289a1d9de11a103d5c69425c9554a2"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/28/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 3, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/28/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Use `str` rather than `repr`. For floats they give the same result in Python 3, but `str` also handles `Decimal` and `int` inputs (`repr(Decimal(...))` is `\"Decimal('\u2026')\"`).\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`. The new test file passes, and so does the existing `test_split`. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the test functions directly with `python3`.\n\n**Why it was wrong:** `round(x, 2)` failed in two ways:\n1. The float `2.675` is really stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so it always rounded down.\n2. Python's `round()` rounds halves to the nearest even digit, so even exact halves go the wrong way: `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`. The docstring already promised \"half up\".\n\n**Fix** in `pricing/money.py`: the value is turned into its shortest decimal text first (`2.675`, not the binary value), then rounded half up with Python's `Decimal`. It still returns a float, so callers don't change, and `add_vat` picks up the fix automatically. Checked results: `2.675 \u2192 2.68`, `1.005 \u2192 1.01`, `0.125 \u2192 0.13`, `-2.675 \u2192 -2.68` (halves round away from zero), `2.674 \u2192 2.67`.\n\n**New tests:** `tests/test_round_money.py` covers each of those cases plus `add_vat`.\n\n**Two remaining risks, not fixed:**\n- `add_vat` rounds `x * 1.2` as a float. If that multiplication lands just below a half (something like `\u20264999999998`), it will still round down. To fully avoid that, prices would need to be kept as `Decimal` or whole cents throughout.\n- `split()` uses `int(total * 100)`, which cuts off instead of rounding. For example `0.29 * 100` is `28.999\u2026`, which becomes `28` cents. That's a separate bug in the same file; I can fix it if you want.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 25252